text Most of the garden is still in the shade.
text I step into the grass, dampening my pants with the morning dew.
text I startle a white butterfly near my feet and it flaps away over the roof.
text I stand next to the rusted garden table.
text I look around.
text I let out a sigh.
text Even in the morning sunlight, the garden looks like an uncivilized grassland.
text At least there are still some flowers left near the hedge.
