music BGM16B.mp3
text Because I kept my face down the whole day, the reddish sun seems too bright to me.
text I gaze at the sunset for a while.
text My back and arms feel heavy, as if filled with lead. My throat is completely dry.
text I look around at the results of the day's work.
text The conspicuous weeds are all gone and about half of the lawn is cut.
text All of the refuse is collected in a corner of the garden.
text It looks much different from this morning.
text But I still don't feel any sense of accomplishment.
text Even though I worked the entire day, it's still far from the garden of my memory.
text I start to hear the sounds of nighttime insects. They seem louder than yesterday.
text @[Tomoya]
text You're gonna get this loud even after I cut so much down?
text I curse at them for no reason.
text The grass I spent so much energy cutting will just go back to the way it was in a few days.
text I stick the hedge clippers into the ground and wipe the sweat from my neck.
text @[Tomoya]
text There's still tomorrow.
text I say that to psyche myself up, but my voice is drowned out by the insects.
text @[Tomoya]
text Tomorrow, huh...
text I look at Kotomi's house, rising in the dim light.
text The dark glass that blocks off the living room is as unchanging as a mural.
text There's still no light coming from the second floor.
text It must be pitch black inside.
text I look around once more.
text Interspersed among the erratically overgrown grass are patches of darkness.
text Evil thoughts are crawling out.
text I came to this garden numerous times as a child.
text Even after listening to Kotomi's story, I don't remember very much from back then.
text It's like some dark red scab blocks my memory.
text Do I even want to remember?
text So what if I do remember?
text It won't bring anything back.
text My younger self is nowhere to be found.
text Kotomi's happiness is nowhere to be found, either.
text I might only be doing this for my own satisfaction.
text It might be completely meaningless.
choice Quit|Keep going
setvar intF[1089] = selected
sound 02.aac
setvar intF[1089] - 1
if intF[1089] == 0
	goto s12
fi
goto 16
label s12
text @[Tomoya]
text I should quit.
text I mumble this to myself and pull the hedge clippers from the ground.
text There must be a better way.
text I should go home for now and think about it...
text I know it seems like I'm making excuses...
text But I know the real reason behind this decision.
text I don't like dealing with this place.
text How did I end up feeling this way?
text In what little memory I have of it, this garden used to be the most enjoyable place in the world.
text I shrug on my jacket and start putting away the tools.
text Driven by the deepening darkness, I work quickly.
